imud (1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * TCP outputs: optional TCP listeners for NMEA ([nmea] tcp_enabled, port
    10110 — chartplotter apps connect directly) and the framed binary
    stream ([stream] tcp_enabled, port 10112 — remote imud-mon/bridge/
    libimud consumers), alongside the existing UDP/AF_UNIX transports.
  * BEHAVIOR CHANGE: built-in defaults now enable only the local AF_UNIX
    stream socket (nmea.enabled true -> false, stream.enabled false ->
    true). Installs relying on the old NMEA-on default must set
    [nmea] enabled = true; the shipped imud.conf already carried this
    posture since 1.5.
  * The Python client gains a TCP mode (ImudClient.connect_tcp / --tcp).

