imud (1.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix two C11 data races: the hot-reload/live
    navigation values are now published under a lock and read via snapshot
    (fusion/reader threads) or atomics (output rates); the stream shutdown
    packet is sent by the stream thread itself (single-owner client list).
  * Validate gpsd/Signal K numeric input: reject NaN/Inf, truncated numbers,
    and out-of-range lat/lon before they reach the filter.
  * Log pthread failures via the returned error code, not errno.
  * SIGHUP now applies heave_tau_s/wave_tau_s/mag_yaw_only (previously
    dropped). New ThreadSanitizer concurrency test in CI.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Wed, 15 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700

imud (1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Black-box recording ([capture] -> rotating .imucap files) and sim-driver
    replay (imud --replay); imud-cal gains offline characterize (Allan
    variance -> cal.json "noise" section, informational only: the filter
    keeps its tuned mekf_* values) and fit-temp (gyro bias/temperature
    compensation) modes.
  * Fix sim-driver pitch-axis mirror between accel/mag and gyro outputs;
    fix mag reader fusing a stale sample when DRDY was not ready.
  * Fix IMU die temperature always reading 25.0 degC (ISM330DHCX/LSM6DSO
    never enabled FIFO temperature batching) — affected packet temp_c,
    imud-mon, the MQTT/InfluxDB/Prometheus telemetry and libimud's
    imud_data_t.temp_c, and made gyro thermal compensation a no-op.
  * Uncalibrated startup: align heading from the uncalibrated magnetometer
    rather than assuming forward = north, and stop counting phantom FIFO
    overflows while awaiting the first mag sample.
  * Report over-long config values instead of silently truncating them.
  * imud-mon moved to the new imud-utils package.
  * Cross-thread stop flags are now C11 _Atomic (ThreadSanitizer-clean).

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Sun, 12 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0700

